LC 350 — Intersection of Two Arrays II
Pattern:Hashing — Frequency Map

Logic:
Count frequency of elements in nums1.
Traverse nums2.
If number exists → add it and decrease its count.

Algorithm:
Count nums1
Check nums2
If count > 0:
    add number
    decrease count

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> intersect(vector<int>& a, vector<int>& b) {
        unordered_map<int,int> mp;
        vector<int> ans;

        for (int x : a) mp[x]++;

        for (int x : b) {
            if (mp[x] > 0) {
                ans.push_back(x);
                mp[x]--;
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};

EX:
nums1 = [1,2,2,1]
nums2 = [2,2]

2 → count = 2 → add
2 → count = 1 → add

Answer = [2,2] ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(n + m)
Space: O(n)
